E
scroll warning~
The Royal Palace is not a place to tread lightly.
  With Warlord and Emperor Zanzen away in battle against the Infidels of
Alden, by decree of Prince Yu-Hin, any person caught inside the Royal
Palace without a proper escort and by invitation of the Prince himself will be
considered an assassin and executed on the spot. Do not move beyond this point
unless you are sure that you are powerful enough or with a group powerful
enough to defeat the numerous guards that inhabit this palace.

 -Nameless
~
#6045
book empire history~
a book of the empire's history~
This book has some background on this strange new land.~
~
13 0 1 0
0 0 0 0
1 500 0
E
book empire history~
This book contains the history of the Empire under the Hajagn dynasty.
 1000 BH (Before Hajagn):
The land was filled with horrible creatures that sought to destroy us. These
creatures controlled all of what we know call home and civilized. The brute
orcs, ogres, and lizardmen ravaged our people and destroyed all we had hoped
to build. Under Chen Hajagn, the first of our most divine dynasty, the city of
Bazabel was first built. Little more than an armored camp, this city gave hope
to all of us who lived in fear of these creatures.
750 BH:
The city of Bazabel becomes a mighty city-state, defending our kind from the
brutes and allowing us to prosper. Xanxen Hajagn becomes the ruler of Bazabel.
 500 BH:
Under Xanxen Hajagn III the first true army of Bazabel is created and the
great purging begins.  The orcs, ogres, and trolls are slaughtered and their
warlords defeated.  Using them as a source of labor, Bazabel reaches a greater
size and defense. Also the founding of Sahardin, our port and outpost against
further raids by these horrid creatures.
200 BH:
The war against the lizards is over and our nation emerges victorious.  The
brutes are pushed back into their own swaps and forever defeated. The gnome
and dwarf's are eradicated, retreating deep into their mountains to avoid our
wrath.
100 BH:
Our great nation becomes a true Empire as we settle every heathen city that is
left. The house of Hajagn is appointed by the people to be the true rulers of
the Empire. It becomes apparent by all that they are chosen by the most divine
to rule and protect us.
0 AH:
The birth of our most glorious and greatest  leader, Zanzen.
5 AH:
The ghoul and elf menace begin their war against us. Our armies begin the
great hunt, crushing all of them that do not swear allegiance to our great
ruler.
25 AH:
Our ships discover another land mass to the west. Reports come back of a
continent inhabited by mostly ghouls and elves.
40 AH:  Emperor Zanzen marshals the greatest army ever assembled to destroy
and
conquer this realm of the damned.  The most blessed Yu-Hin assumes temporary
control of the Empire while he glorious father seeks to further safe-guard us
all from these evils.
~
#6046
scroll hero tales~
a scroll of hero's tales.~
This scroll depicts great stories of heroism.~
~
13 0 1 0
0 0 0 0
1 500 0
E
scroll hero tale~
This scroll contains stories of several heroes of the Empire.


"Liu-Xen, one of the great lords of the dynasty Hajagn, was a man no
taller than you or I, yet his strength was greater than any orc. He lead
our forces against the orc hordes that for so long had raped our women,
burned out fields, and killed our sons. Liu-Xen took a party of no more
than 50 men, most of them farmers and shepherds and went to do battle
with the greatest orc chieftain, Zalen. These brave souls were out-matched,
out numbered, and starving, but this band of 50 men slaughtered over
500 orcs in glorious battle.  Zalen himself was slain by Liu-Xen, his head
brought back to our great city has a trophy and warning to the other
barbarian races, We are no longer slaves.
~
#6047
essay lesser creature~
an essay on lesser creatures~
This essay is written bout the other races.~
~
13 0 1 0
0 0 0 0
1 500 0
E
essay lesser creature~
The Elf is a creature who is well endowed with the powers of witchcraft
and the black arts. While they are often smaller than us, the most
perfect of all creatures, their ruthlessness and wicked minds help them
charm and train other larger beasts to do their bidding. They are the
most true sign of evil in the world and only those select few that allow
the protection of Zanzen to overtake them can be saved.

The Orc, Ogre, and Troll are their bastard offspring are simple creatures.
Their slow minds and lack of true thought make them more akin to
cattle than a true creature. Their great size and weak minds make
them ideal workers and because of our control over them we have
made cities that no man could ever hope to duplicate them. They are
best culled to keep their numbers low but are necessary for our
further expansion.

The lizardman or lizard is a creature  that must also be eradicated. These
creatures, while primitive, still contain a larger degree of thought that
the other brute races.  Their speed, agility, and lack of any morals
make them dangerous creatures that love only chaos and thus,
for all of our safety, be killed.

The gnome and dwarf are creatures that cannot be trusted. While some
are free to walk in our cities, and their ability to produce complex
technology make them useful for designing cities and weapons, they
must be under constant supervision. Even know many of them align
themselves with those last few rebel ghouls and elves.  Never trust
them.

The Pixies have long since aided us. In the dark days it was their healing
magic and their knowledge that allowed us to defend our home
and eventually establish our great cities. They are small, but their
magical ability is unsurpassed as is their critical thinking skills. Truly,
our greatest ally and the only other creature we have encountered
worthy of any respect.  While they are useful indeed, their small
size makes them inferior to us.

The Ghouls are creatures of pure hatred and destruction. Not much is known
about these creatures as they have hidden from us for so long. We
have great reason to believe it was them that organized the brute creatures
into such armies and it was indeed their will to destroy us. They must
be found and killed or else we shall always live in peril.
~
